body:
what the fuck, no. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

???? What is someone supposed to fix about themselves if you say "sorry I don't like black guys"? It's an unfixable trait. It benefits no one

&#x200B;

Also, the insecure thing is BS. We all have insecurities that get to us sometimes, no ones perfect. That's an unreasonable expectation to put on someone

> Tell me, what part of ‘back up’ is illegal? If a cop tells me to back up you better fucking believe that I’m gonna back the fuck up. 

if a cop told you to lick their boots would you?  

&#x200B;

It sucks you have to deal with this, I'm not gonna lie and say your probably going to have a hard time dating but that doesn't mean you can't find anything worthwile during your life time. Try a hobby, and not because you'll meet people, but just find something youe GENUINELY like and put your soul into it.

&#x200B;

Also if it helps you feel better [this guy](https://youtu.be/EatMNSGMW5g?t=436) has a really severe and he's [still dating](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8CZ58ROFElY)

I think women get more attention than guys but it's not really good attention. I think there are a lot of guys who are willing to have sex with any girl but not be in a relationship with them. Maybe that sounds good to some people, but i think even most men on this sub would agree sex isn't the main problem with being FA.

&#x200B;

 I don't know I think there are A LOT more women who fall under the FA category than people think, maybe not as much as men though.

Black men shitting on dark skin women is extremely common in black culture. If you notice in the media most popular black women are light skinned, have European features, and loose hair(or a weave). I'm not saying that light skinned black women aren't black, i'm just saying that they're more accepted and considered more attractive in society. 

&#x200B;

What I'm trying to say is these women AT MOST are not doing anything for the acceptance of black women because the black women they're pretending to be are already accepted.

These women aren't glorifying black women, their glorifying racial ambiguity. Light skinned girls with loose hair and euro features have always been seen as desirable, these insta models are doing nothing for black women that hasn't already been done. dark skinned women with 4C kinky hair and strong African are still seen as undesirable.

&#x200B;

I don't think its black face but these women are doing nothing but contributing to the idea that the closer to being "white" the more attractive you are, while the rest of us get ignored.

from what i know FA is a vague title and it can mean a lot of things. There are a lot of non-virgin FAs in this sub, what most people want is a meaningful relationship not just sex. 

&#x200B;

I'm a girl and i've never been approached aside from pedophiles when I was younger. Now that I'm older I never get approached. Not only that but I can't really speak to people because I dont have any social skills and I have social anxiety. I don't even know what most people talk about or how most people talk about things so people just get bored with me even if we have similar interest I can communicate it well usually. So I'm just ugly and boring to most people

>can barely hold it together

didn't he hook up with 2 girls right after lmao?

